    "summary": "High‑energy ’73 show: Big River, epic Playing In The Band→Other One, crisp China→Rider.",
    "blurb": "Features a blistering Big River, a monster Playing In The Band into The Other One marathon, and a flawless China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider sequence. Jerry’s guitar shines throughout while the rhythm section drives the high‑octane jams. All recordings are excellent, with the Miller soundboard offering pristine clarity.",
    "review": "The July 1, 1973 Universal Amphitheatre concert captures the Dead in top form, riding a wave of relentless momentum from start to finish. The first set builds nicely through classics before exploding on a scorching Big River where Jerry’s lead work is nothing short of incendiary. A seamless China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider segue highlights the band’s tight interplay and Keith’s tasteful keys. The second set launches into a monster Playing In The Band that morphs into an extended Other One marathon, eventually spilling over into a soaring Truckin' → The Other One → Wharf Rat suite that showcases Phil’s bass in overdrive and the dual drummers locking down a powerful groove. Loose Lucy provides a brief, relaxed breather before the band closes with Row Jimmy, El Paso, and a joyous Casey Jones. Across all sources the Miller soundboard capture stands out for its crystal‑clear mix, but even the audience tapes convey the night’s high energy and flawless execution.",
